SELECT 'Mountain hiking', 'Eight weeks to climb and come back down unharmed: braking leg strength, hills and stairs, outings of 400 to 1,000 m of climbing.', 'endurance', 'intermediate', 3, true, '[{"name":"W1 · Strength","week":1,"exercises":[{"exerciseName":"Bulgarian Split Squat","targetSets":3,"targetReps":"8-10","restSec":90},{"exerciseName":"Step-up","targetSets":4,"targetReps":"10-12","restSec":60},{"exerciseName":"Single-Leg Romanian Deadlift","targetSets":3,"targetReps":"8-10","restSec":75},{"exerciseName":"Reverse Lunge","targetSets":3,"targetReps":"10-12","restSec":60},{"exerciseName":"Single-Leg Calf Raise","targetSets":3,"targetReps":"12-15","restSec":45},{"exerciseName":"Plank","targetSets":3,"targetReps":"30-45s","restSec":45}]},{"name":"W1 · Hills and stairs","week":1,"exercises":[],"cardio":{"sport":"hike","durationMin":49,"intensity":"Zone 3-4","purpose":"Climb with breath and power, then come down under control.","steps":["Warm-up: 10 min of easy walking, then ankle and hip circles","4 climbs of 3 min at a good pace (hill or stairs), walking slowly back down","Cool-down: 5 to 10 min of slow walking, then calf and thigh stretches"],"notes":"Poles spare the knees downhill and help uphill: set them at elbow height."}},{"name":"W1 · Outing with climbing","week":1,"exercises":[],"cardio":{"sport":"hike","durationMin":180,"intensity":"Zone 2","purpose":"Climb at a pace you can hold for long, and spare the knees on the way down.","steps":["Warm-up: 10 min of easy walking, then ankle and hip circles","About 400 m of climbing over 3 h, steady pace uphill","Downhill: short steps, soft knees, poles if you have them","Cool-down: 5 to 10 min of slow walking, then calf and thigh stretches"],"notes":"Brake on the descents: that is where knees and thighs suffer most. Eat a little every hour and drink before you are thirsty. Before you go: route left with someone, weather checked, water, food, a warm layer, a first-aid kit and a charged phone."}},{"name":"W2 · Str